{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"asbestine-inaccurate-sanderling","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Problem\nAn MCP `review_plan_start` job for ticket `unadhesive-erectable-axolotl` changed from `running` to `stale-running` without writing a readable `REVIEW_RESULT` sidecar or a plan-review attestation.\n\n## Observed\n- Date: 2026-09-04.\n- Job: `1788538783977524160-fd43d54af972425e89d256830684fdf6`.\n- Initial `review_plan_start` returned a normal running handle.\n- The first `gate_status` poll reported `running`, `findings.readable=false`, and an unsigned durable result.\n- The next poll reported `stale-running`, `findings.reason=run-stale-running`, and no signature.\n- An immediately preceding review job on the same ticket completed normally with a structural BLOCK.\n\n## Expected\nThe async daemon records a terminal PASS/BLOCK/ERROR result and readable diagnostic evidence, or the MCP surface returns an actionable cause for the daemon death.\n\n## Reproduction\nEdit a plan after a structural plan-review BLOCK, call `review_plan_start` again for `origin/main`, and poll the returned job with `gate_status`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The daemon-death cause is reproducible or identified from durable evidence.\n- [ ] A stale async gate records an actionable terminal error or recoverable diagnostic evidence.\n- [ ] Regression coverage exercises the stale-running path without a billable external model call.","id":"17e5-d776-31b8-40ba","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["mcp","plan-review","reliability"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP async plan-review job loses result as stale-running"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788538948128699712,"uuid":"61e53aaa-c0f0-46c3-b929-1cc10a19e132"}